JPL CODEC — REPOSITORY INSTRUCTION DOCUMENT (Claude Code Setup Spec)

This document defines the canonical structure, governance, and deployment spine for the JPL Codec system across:

GitHub (code + versioned grammar + CLI tools)

Supabase (state, telemetry, benchmarks, model outputs)


It explicitly inherits architectural constraints from JARVIS governance principles and the YGGDRASIL hierarchical memory model.


---

1. SYSTEM IDENTITY

Project Name

JPL CODEC

Purpose

A cross-model reasoning compiler system that:

Encodes natural language into graph IR (JPL)

Compares outputs across models (GPT / Gemini / Claude)

Computes structural divergence metrics

Builds consensus graphs from reasoning traces



---

2. CORE ARCHITECTURAL PRINCIPLES (JARVIS-INHERITED)

2.1 Governance Spine (JARVIS MODEL)

All system components must obey:

Single source of truth per layer

No implicit state mutation

All transformations must be traceable

No duplication of semantic responsibility

Strict separation of:

Encoding (E0)

Evaluation (Δ / CSF engine)

Storage (Supabase)

Execution (CLI / API layer)




---

2.2 Hierarchical Memory Spine (YGGDRASIL MODEL)

System is organized as a tree of controlled abstraction layers:

ROOT (YGGDRASIL)
│
├── 0. CORE IR LAYER (JPL GRAPH MODEL)
│
├── 1. ENCODERS (E0 family)
│
├── 2. DECODERS (D0 family)
│
├── 3. METRICS ENGINE (Δ / Ω / CSF)
│
├── 4. CONSENSUS ENGINE (JPL-Σ)
│
├── 5. BENCHMARK HARNESS (multi-model testing)
│
├── 6. STORAGE LAYER (Supabase)
│
└── 7. INTERFACE LAYER (CLI / API / future UI)

Rule:

No lower layer may depend on higher layers.


