3.2 Design Rules (STRICT)

No cross-folder circular dependencies

All metrics must be stateless functions

All graph transformations must be deterministic

CLI must be the ONLY entry point for execution

Supabase is read/write state only (never logic)



---

4. SUPABASE ARCHITECTURE (STATE LAYER)

4.1 Database Name

jpl_codec_db


---

4.2 Tables

4.2.1 models

Stores model metadata.

model_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY
name TEXT
version TEXT
capabilities JSONB


---

4.2.2 runs

Each benchmark execution.

run_id UUID PRIMARY KEY
timestamp TIMESTAMP
input_hash TEXT
mode TEXT (LOSSLESS | PARAPHRASE | ADVERSARIAL)


---

4.2.3 jpl_outputs

Stores encoded graphs per model.

output_id UUID
run_id UUID
model_id TEXT
jpl_graph JSONB
token_count INT


---

4.2.4 diff_results

Stores comparison outputs.

diff_id UUID
run_id UUID
csf_score FLOAT
delta2 FLOAT
delta3 FLOAT
delta4 FLOAT
omega FLOAT
entropy JSONB


---

4.2.5 consensus_graphs

Stores merged outputs.

consensus_id UUID
run_id UUID
graph JSONB
confidence FLOAT


---

4.3 Supabase Rules

No logic execution in SQL

No graph transformation in DB

Only storage + retrieval

All computation happens in GitHub layer



---

5. CLI SPEC (PRIMARY INTERFACE)

Commands

jpl encode input.txt
jpl decode graph.json
jpl diff gpt.json gemini.json
jpl run benchmark --mode adversarial
jpl consensus run
jpl score run_id


---

CLI Flow

input → encoder → graph → metrics → diff → supabase store → report


